  "2": {
    "inputs": {
      "value": "subject_definitions:\n<Subject 1> is the character defined by the character sheet in <Picture 1>. The sheet provides her identity and wardrobe throughout the video.\n\nsummary:\n[reference generation] Create a 10-second photorealistic pottery-studio scene featuring <Subject 1>. She pulls wet clay too high on a spinning pottery wheel, watches it collapse, reacts with surprise, then laughs at the mistake. She reshapes the clay into a small open vessel and proudly brings it close to the camera.\n\nretention_analysis:\n<Subject 1> (appears throughout [Shot 1]): fully_preserved - consistently maintain the identity and wardrobe established by <Picture 1>. Allow realistic clay residue on her hands and small incidental splashes during the pottery work.\n\ndetailed_description:\nA photorealistic cinematic lifestyle scene, 10 seconds, 16:9. A bright pottery studio has wooden shelves filled with handmade ceramic bowls, cups, and unfinished vessels. Tools and clay supplies occupy nearby worktables. Soft window daylight illuminates the workspace. A pottery wheel and its clay-splattered splash pan fill the lower foreground.\n\n[Shot 1] One continuous, nearly stationary medium shot from across the wheel, keeping <Subject 1>'s face, both hands, and the clay visible. Use natural real-time gestures and readable changes in expression.\n\nFrom 0 to 3 seconds, <Subject 1> leans forward with an eager smile, cupping a wet clay form between both slippery hands as the wheel rotates. She draws her hands upward, pulling the clay into an increasingly tall, narrow shape. Her expression becomes uncertain as the upper section begins to wobble.\n\nThe clay bends off-center, folds sideways, and slumps onto the rotating wheel. She immediately separates her hands from it, lifting both muddy palms clear. Preserve the clay's soft material behavior: it folds and compresses rather than shattering or disappearing.\n\nFrom 3 to 5 seconds, she stares at the collapsed clay with widened eyes and parted lips, hands still suspended above the wheel. After a brief surprised pause, she glances toward the camera and breaks into a spontaneous grin. Her shoulders relax as she laughs visibly, then she looks down and returns both hands toward the clay.\n\nFrom 5 to 8 seconds, she gathers the slumped material toward the wheel's center and compresses it into a shorter, sturdier form. One hand supports the outside while the fingers of the other open the center and gently widen the mouth. As the wheel turns, the clay develops into a small cup-shaped bowl with a thick base, softly rounded walls, and a slightly uneven rim.\n\nKeep the vessel modest and handmade. Show continuous hand contact, concentric throwing marks, and a wet surface sheen. She finishes smoothing the rim, lifts her shaping fingers clear, and smiles at the result.\n\nFrom 8 to 10 seconds, the wheel slows as she carefully lifts the vessel free, supporting its base with one palm and steadying the side with the other. Once it is secure, she brings it toward the lens in one hand, tilting the opening forward so the interior and circular throwing marks become clearly visible.\n\nShe opens her other clay-covered palm beside it in a playful presentation gesture and looks directly at the camera with a delighted smile. The vessel grows large in the foreground and partly obscures her torso while her face remains visible beside it. End at 10 seconds on this proud, cheerful display.\n\noverall_soundscape:\nN/A\n\nnon_diegetic_music:\nN/A"
    },
    "class_type": "PrimitiveStringMultiline",
    "_meta": {
      "title": "\u63d0\u793a\u8bcd"
    }
  },
